  "conclusions": [
    "The common checker dispatcher mutates one shared fixture checkout and cannot simply run concurrently.",
    "Baseline changes during fixture construction; any immutable queue must capture each exact B/H rather than read a later closure value.",
    "Actual validator worktree bytes are deliberately changed by required-date, delayed-clock regression and missing-status-message mutants; checking out only B in a queued worker would lose those controls.",
